The Following is a list of ToolTypes for this ICON:


NOTICE: ALL TOOLTYPES ARE CASE SENSITIVE

ABOUT: This ICON may be any name you wish it to be. You should find some
       pre-defined NRAM.DEFS in the STORAGE/NRAMS directory.

       This defines the commands your particular modem requires to perform
       setting the NRAMS.

       This ICON may be in the NODE/NRAMS directory for any node which is
       tied to a modem.


NRAM.<num>=


NRAM.<num>=<string>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells /X what command to send to the modem to set NRAMS
         -<num> is the nth occurance of the NRAM tooltype.

     NRAM.1=ATZ
     NRAM.2=AT&A3&K3&G2
     NRAM.3=AT&W
     NRAM.4=ATZ

